      "description": "Presiding Deity : Lord Brahma, Lord Vishnu, Lord Shiva Beej Mantra : Om Namah: Benefits : &nbsp;For effective leadership and complete success. Origin : Nepal Description: What is the Trijuti Rudraksha? The Trijuti Rudraksha is a rare and magnificent bead that consists of three Rudrakshas naturally joined together, representing the trinity of Brahma, Vishnu, and Mahesh. This Rudraksha bestows universal appeal, great achievements, and spiritual progress on the wearer. The ruling deities of the Trijuti Rudraksha are Lords Brahma, Vishnu, and Mahesh(Shiva), the creator, preserver, and destroyer of the universe. Wearing this Rudraksha brings the grace of the supreme trinity, who are the source of all knowledge, wisdom, and power. Wearing this Rudraksha is also considered to be a sign of good fortune and divine protection. Different ways to wear a Trijuti Mukhi Rudraksha The Trijuti Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The Trijuti Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The Trijuti Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combination like the Indra mala. A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Lords Brahma, Vishnu, and Mahesh were the three supreme gods of the universe, who were responsible for the creation, preservation, and destruction respectively. They were also the manifestations of the one Supreme Being, Brahman. They decided to test their powers and create their worlds, with different laws, beings, and paths. Lord Brahma created a world of beauty and harmony, with the Vedas, the Varnas, the Devas, and the Asuras. &nbsp;Lord Vishnu created a world of compassion and justice, with the dharma, the Yugas, the Avataras, and the Bhaktas. Lord Shiva created a world of passion and transformation, with the tantra, the chakras, the rudras, and the yogis. They watched over their creations and visited each other’s worlds. They exchanged gifts and compliments and learned from each other. They lived in harmony and friendship and respected each other’s roles and responsibilities. They are still the supreme Gods of the universe and are still the manifestations of the one Supreme Being, Brahman.",
      "benefits": "Here are some of the many benefits of wearing the Trijuti Rudraksha: General Benefits: Wearing it brings the blessings of the Vedic Trinity and makes the wearer a complete personality who can command any situation. It is perfect for effective leadership and complete success. It is also a vital component of the Indramala, a powerful combination of Rudrakshas. Spiritual Benefits: The bead draws the grace of all deities and connects the wearer to the consciousness of Brahma, Vishnu, and Mahesh. It helps the wearer overcome any adverse situation and ensures success in material and spiritual life. It is auspicious to keep it in the place of worship.",
      "whoShouldWear": "Who can wear the Trijuti Rudraksha? The Trijuti Rudraksha is suitable for anyone who wants to enjoy these benefits and live a prosperous life. However, it is especially beneficial for people who are in the following categories: For spiritual enlightenment and liberation by connecting with the Trinity. Those seeking success and innovation by enhancing intelligence, creativity, and leadership can wear it. People seeking protection and happiness by overcoming negative energies, evil forces, and diseases should wear them. One can wear it for harmony and balance by harmonizing your body, mind, and soul, and balancing the three gunas.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash and oil your Rudraksha with almond oil monthly using a soft brush and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing it the next day. Remove it during sexual intercourse and funeral visits. You can remove it while eating non-vegetarian food or drinking alcohol and wear it again later. Women can wear it all the time, even during their menstrual cycles. To energize it, touch it to a Shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. Perform a Rudrabhishek of it when possible. Do not wear or use a Rudraksha Mala worn by others. Keep a separate Mala for Japa and for wearing."
