      "description": "Presiding Deity : Shiv Parvati Beej Mantra: Om Gaurishankaraya Namah Benefits : Building strong relationships and bringing marital happiness Origin : Nepal Description: What is the Gaurishankar Rudraksha? The Gaurishankar Rudraksha is a special bead that consists of two naturally joined Rudrakshas, symbolizing the union and companionship of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati. This Rudraksha brings harmony, happiness, and prosperity in relationships, especially marriage. The ruling planet of the Gaurishankar Rudraksha is the Moon, the planet of emotions, mind, and creativity. The ruling deity of the Gaurishankar Rudraksha is Shiv Shakti, the divine couple that represents the balance of masculine and feminine energies. Wearing this Rudraksha attracts the grace of both, Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati, making it a promising choice for anyone seeking to enhance their love and devotion. The Gaurishankar Rudraksha is available in large and collector sizes. Different ways to wear the Gaurishankar Rudraksha The Gaurishankar Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The Gaurishankar Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The Gaurishankar Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combinations like the Gaurishankar Kantha, Indra Mala, Siddha mala, or the Maha Mrityunjay mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Shiva and Shakti were the supreme couple of the universe, but they had different interests and personalities. Shakti, as Parvati, tried to win Shiva’s love by serving him, but he ignored her. She then performed a severe penance, which impressed Shiva, but he tested her faith by sending a messenger to discourage her. Parvati remained loyal and devoted, and Shiva revealed himself and asked her to marry him. They celebrated their wedding and became one in body, mind, and soul. They lived happily ever after, as Shiva and Shakti, the divine couple of the universe.",
      "benefits": "The Gaurishankar Rudraksha is a special bead that symbolizes the union of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati. This Rudraksha brings harmony, happiness, and prosperity in relationships, especially marriage. Here are some of the benefits of wearing the Gaurishankar Rudraksha: General Benefits: Wearing it improves and heals relationships, brings marital happiness, and helps to find the right partner. It also promotes peace and harmony with family. Spiritual Benefits: The bead calms the mind, reduces stress, and enhances decision-making. It is ruled by the Moon, the planet of emotions and intuition. Health Benefits: It is beneficial for cough, cold, and chest problems. It strengthens the respiratory system and immunity.",
      "whoShouldWear": "A Gaurishankar rudraksha is suitable for anyone who wants to enjoy these benefits and live a prosperous life. However, it is especially beneficial for people who are in the following categories: For love and harmony in your marriage or to find your soulmate. A person seeking spiritual growth and enlightenment by balancing your energies can wear it. One can also wear it for success, prosperity, and abundance by overcoming obstacles. One can wear it for health and well-being by calming your mind and healing your body.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash and oil your Rudraksha with almond oil monthly using a soft brush and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing it the next day. Remove it during sexual intercourse and funeral visits. You can remove it while eating non-vegetarian food or drinking alcohol and wear it again later. Women can wear it all the time, even during their menstrual cycles. To energize it, touch it to a Shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. Perform a Rudrabhishek of it when possible. Do not wear or use a Rudraksha Mala worn by others. Keep a separate Mala for Japa and for wearing."
