      "description": "Presiding Deity: Lord Ram Ruling Planet: Rahu Beej Mantra: Om Namah Shivay Benefits: For victory against enemies and court cases. Origin: Nepal Description: What is the 16 Mukhi Rudraksha? The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha is a rare and powerful bead with sixteen natural lines or facets on its surface. It is a talisman of a virtuous human being who’s endowed with tremendous fortitude. It is blessed by Lord Rama and Lord Mahakaal and is ruled by the planet Rahu. It bestows the wearer with good family relationships, respect, fame, and success. It protects the wearer from theft, cheating, and enemies. It removes the fear of death and unfounded fears. It helps overcome unfavorable planetary positions and chronic diseases. It is beneficial for people involved in the land and construction business, industrialists, and high-authority professionals. It is a highly valued and auspicious bead that brings benefits to all the Rudraksha beads from 1 to 14 Mukhi. The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha is available in large, collector, and super collector sizes.&nbsp; About the ruling planet Rahu Rahu is a planet that has a lot of influence on human life, but it is not a physical planet. It is a point where the moon's orbit intersects with the ecliptic, the apparent path of the sun. Rahu is also known as the northern lunar node or the dragon's head in Vedic astrology. Rahu can bring sudden changes, innovation, curiosity, and ambition into one's life. However, it can also cause illusion, confusion, deception, and addiction if it is afflicted or ill-placed. Rahu can be pacified by worshipping Lord Shiva, Goddess Durga, Lord Ganesha, or Lord Hanuman, and by chanting the Rahu Mantra or the Rahu Beej Mantra. Rahu can also be balanced and harmonized by wearing a Rudraksha bead that corresponds to its number, such as the 8 Mukhi Rudraksha or the 16 Mukhi Rudraksha. Different ways to wear a 16 Mukhi Rudraksha The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combinations like the Indra mala, the Siddha mala, or the Maha Mrityunjay mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Lord Rama was born into a royal family and grew up to be a virtuous, courageous, and righteous prince. The young prince was also physically very strong. He was the only one who could lift and string a bow during the Swayamvar of Devi Sita. He won her hand in marriage and returned to Ayodhya. This young scion of the Ikshvaku dynasty was fate's chosen child. Due to a promise given by his father, he was exiled into the forest for 14 years. He honored this promise and lived in the forest with his brother Lakshman and his wife Sita. When Sita was abducted by Ravana, Lord Rama was heartbroken. He received the aid of Lord Hanuman, an Anshavatar of Lord Shiva. The legion of monkeys helped Lord Rama build a bridge across the ocean to reach Lanka where Sita was imprisoned. Lord Rama had to wage a war and kill Ravana to get Sita Devi back. He returned to Ayodhya with his wife and was crowned the King amidst cries of victorious cries of “Jai Shri Ram”. The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha is an extremely powerful and rare bead. It controls the malefic effects of the planet Rahu. This shadow planet is known for its illusory and deceptive powers. The energy of the 16 Mukhi can cut through any illusion, or deceit and bestow the wearer with auspiciousness. Victory and happiness follow the wearer. These lines from Ramashtakam mention this.",
      "benefits": "The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha is a type of bead with 16 natural lines on its surface and is believed to have various benefits for the wearer. It is associated with Lord Shiva, the destroyer of evil, and Lord Ram, the ideal king and warrior. Here are some of the benefits of wearing the 16 Mukhi Rudraksha: General Benefits: This bead gives victory over legal issues, respect, fame, and victory. It protects against deceit, cheating, and theft. It boosts self-esteem and removes fear of death. Spiritual Benefits: This bead activates the Mooladhara / Base Chakra. It increases the grounding energy. The wearer becomes practical, grounded, and fulfills worldly obligations. The wearer faces life challenges with calmness and courage. The wearer follows the spiritual path while meeting worldly responsibilities. Health Benefits: This bead helps recover from acute and chronic ailments. It heals kidneys, intestines, lower back, etc. It calms the emotions in stressful and adverse situations.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha is a rare and auspicious bead that can bring success, victory, and protection to the wearer. It is especially beneficial for people who face the following situations or challenges in their life: You are involved in a legal matter or a dispute and want to win the case or resolve the issue in your favor. You are in a business or a profession that requires you to deal with trading, chemical, or pharmaceutical products, and you want to prosper and grow in your field. You are afraid of death, accidents, diseases, or enemies, and you want to avoid any harm or danger that may come your way. You are influenced by the planet Rahu, which can cause sudden changes, illusion, confusion, or deception in your life, and you want to balance and harmonize its effects. The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha can also grant you fame, wealth, leadership, and victory in all aspects of life. It can also protect you from any evil or negative influences. The 16 Mukhi Rudraksha is also known as the Jai Rudraksha, as it can make you victorious in every situation.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
