      "description": "Presiding Deity: Lord Kuber Ruling Planet: Venus Beej Mantra: Om Hreem Hum Shivmitraye Namah Benefits: Shields one from evil eye or Tantric effects, retains fortune Origin: Nepal Description: What is the 21 Mukhi Rudraksha? The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha is a very rare and precious bead that has 21 lines or facets on its surface. It represents the power of Venus, the planet of love, beauty, and luxury, and Lord Kuber, the God of wealth and prosperity. This Rudraksha bestows the wearer with immense riches, happiness, and fulfillment. The wearer of this Rudraksha can enjoy all the pleasures of life and attain the highest level of satisfaction. The ruling planet of the 21 Mukhi Rudraksha, Venus, influences the heart, emotions, and relationships, while its association with Lord Kuber enhances abundance, generosity, and success. Wearing this Rudraksha brings the grace of both Venus and Lord Kuber, making it a highly auspicious choice for anyone seeking wealth, love, and bliss. The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha is available in large and collector sizes. About the ruling planet Venus The ruling planet of Venus is Venus itself, which is also known as Shukra or Bhrigu in Vedic astrology. Venus is the planet of love, beauty, harmony, and pleasure. It represents the water element and the color white. Venus governs the signs of Taurus and Libra and the second and seventh houses in the horoscope. Venus can bring romance, happiness, creativity, and artistry to one’s endeavors. However, it can also cause indulgence, vanity, laziness, and jealousy if it is afflicted or ill-placed. The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha helps to balance and harmonize the effects of Venus in one’s horoscope. It can help overcome the challenges and obstacles that Venus may bring, such as lack of self-esteem, insecurity, infidelity, and conflict. It can also help enhance the positive qualities of Venus, such as love, beauty, harmony, and pleasure. Different ways to wear the 21 Mukhi Rudraksha The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combinations like the Indra mala, the Siddha mala, or the Maha Mrityunjay mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Once after a long penance, Lord Kubera opened his eyes. He could not bear the radiant form of Lord Shiva’s blinding effulgence. Lord Shiva then gave him the power to see the divine light. Lord Kubera saw the divine Goddess with his eyes wide open. The Goddess was infuriated by his wide-eyed glance and plucked one of his eyes out. Lord Shiva intervened and blessed him saying that he was in charge of riches and treasury. He was appointed the ruler of Alkapuri.",
      "benefits": "The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha is a bead that brings wealth, prosperity, and spiritual growth to the wearer. It has the following benefits: General Benefits: Wearing it brings enormous wealth and good fortune, protection from evil eye and Tantric effects, and retention of fortune due to Lord Kubera’s blessings. Spiritual Benefits: The bead houses the divine energies of Gods and Goddesses, including Brahma, Vishnu, and Mahesh, and offers health blessings from Lord Dhanvantari, safeguarding against black magic and negative Tantric practices. Health Benefits: It contributes to longevity, and blood sugar control, and alleviates prostate issues, enhancing overall well-being.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 21 Mukhi Rudraksha is suitable for anyone who wants to enjoy these benefits and live a prosperous life. However, it is especially beneficial for people who are in the following categories: People who are involved in land deals, property, real estate business, or any other business related to earth. People who want to fulfill their desires and achieve their goals in life. People who want to overcome the obstacles and challenges in their lives and face them with courage and confidence. People who want to balance their Kapha dosha and improve their health and well-being. People who want to increase their connection with Mother Earth and nature and respect the environment.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
