      "description": "Presiding Deity: Lord Vishwakarma Ruling Planet: Saturn Beej Mantra: Om Namah Shivay Benefits: Good for land and property business; starting of new projects and its success. Origin: Nepal Description: What is the 17 Mukhi Rudraksha? The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha is a rare and powerful bead with seventeen natural lines or facets on its surface. It represents the divine form of Lord Vishwakarma, the celestial architect who is the mystical builder of many celestial kingdoms and weapons. He is an expert in crafting with creativity and splendor. Blessed by Lord Vishwakarma and Goddess Katyayani, these deities bestow the wearer with sudden wealth, heightened spiritual powers, and the four attainments of Dharma, Artha, Kama, and Moksha. The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha is ruled by the planet Saturn, which is also known as the lord of karma and justice. The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha is available in large, collector, and super collector sizes.&nbsp; About the ruling planet Saturn The ruling planet of the 17 Mukhi Rudraksha is Saturn, known as Shani or Sauri in Vedic astrology. Saturn is the planet of discipline, karma, justice, and endurance. It represents the earth element and the color black. Saturn can bring hard work, responsibility, patience, and perseverance to one’s endeavors. However, it can also cause delay, obstruction, sorrow, and misery if it is afflicted or ill-placed. The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha helps balance and harmonize the effects of Saturn in one’s horoscope. It can help overcome the challenges and obstacles that Saturn may bring, such as poverty, debt, disease, and litigation. It can also help enhance the positive qualities of Saturn, such as wealth, success, and longevity. Different ways to wear the 17 Mukhi Rudraksha The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in popular combinations like the Indra mala, the Siddha mala, or the Maha Mrityunjay mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Vishwakarma is the creator of the architectural splendor of the golden city of Lanka. What was originally designed for Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati was eventually given to the Asura King Ravana as Dakshina. When lord Shiva reduced Kamdev to ashes with the fire emitted from his third eye it was Lord Vishwakarma who collected the ashes and made a doll with it. Lord Shiva breathed life into this to give rise to the mighty Bhanda (Bhandasura). When the radiance of Suryadev was too much for his wife to bear, Lord Vishwakarma collected the excess to craft celestial weapons from them thereby making Surya’s radiance bearable. The splendor of magnificent architecture and creativity with a purpose is the blessing of Lord Vishwakarma. The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha encases this magical blessing. Women who wear the 17 Mukhi Rudraksha are blessed with a lovely marital life. It is known to bless them with an appropriate spouse, good children, happiness, and a prolonged life for the spouse. The mantra for Katyayani Devi can be chanted by women to seek her blessings.",
      "benefits": "The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha is a bead that brings wealth, prosperity, and spiritual growth to the wearer. It has the following benefits: General Benefits: It enhances spiritual powers, intuition, and creative intelligence. It attracts wealth from unexpected sources, such as inheritance, lottery, stock market, etc.&nbsp; Spiritual Benefits: It invokes the grace of Lord Vishwakarma, the celestial architect who is the master of creativity and splendor. He helps the wearer to craft his destiny and rule his soul. He guides the wearer to the right path and releases him from the karmic bondage and fear of death. Health Benefits: &nbsp;It is extremely beneficial for bones and nerves. It is also known as Mahamrityunjaya, the conqueror of death.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 17 Mukhi Rudraksha is a sacred bead associated with Goddess Katyayani, the sixth form of Goddess Durga, and Lord Vishvakarma, the architect of the universe. It’ s suitable for anyone who wants to enjoy its benefits and live a king-like life. People who are in a speculative profession, such as betting and lottery. People who are looking for a suitable life partner or want to improve their existing relationship. People who want to overcome the obstacles and challenges in their lives and achieve their goals.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
