      "description": "Number of beads&nbsp;- 108 + 1 Meru Size of beads - 7mm Mala length - approximately 46cms Description - The 7 mm, 5 Mukhi Rudraksha Mala 108 + 1 enables wearers to attain good health, a calm mind, and overall well-being by the power of the 5 Mukhi Rudraksha. This sacred Mala consists of 108 + 1 beads of the 5 Mukhi Rudraksha of Indonesian origin, which are auspicious for wearing, according to ancient Vedic texts. The size of the beads is 7 mm, which is considerably light in weight and sturdy for everyday use. The Mala has beads strung along the thread with a tassel, as tradition dictates. We at Rudralife suggest this Rudraksha Mala for wearing purposes because it brings with it the blessings and protection of Lord Shiva. Configuration - 109 x 5 Mukhi (Indonesian)&nbsp; How to use a Japa Mala: To use a Japa mala, start from the Meru bead and chant 108 times. Do not cross the Meru bead and reverse the mala for the next cycle. Avoid sharing the Japa mala with others for chants.",
      "benefits": "The 5 Mukhi Rudraksha Mala has many benefits for the wearer, both spiritual and material. Some of the benefits are: General Benefits: The wearer of this Rudraksha gets to live life completely, calmly, and fearlessly. It blesses the wearer with good health and peace of mind. The wearer becomes relaxed and stress-free in his daily pursuits and leads a better quality of life. Spiritual Benefits: The Shastras advise wearing this divine seed for a complete Chakra cleansing and re-energizing. The 5 Mukhi Rudraksha connects one to the grace of Lord Shiva and enhances awareness, memory, word power, and intellect. Health Benefits: The 5 Mukhi Rudraksha Mala is good for the circulation of blood and also keeps blood pressure in check. The Pali variety of this bead is effective in chronic coughs, colds, and sinusitis. It is ideal for good health, and peace of mind, and safeguards the wearer from untimely death.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 5 Mukhi rudraksha mala can be worn by anyone who wants to improve their life in various aspects. There are no restrictions over who can wear this bead. However, some people who may benefit more from wearing the 5 Mukhi Rudraksha are: Those suffering from the negative effects of Jupiter in their horoscope, such as a lack of wisdom, wealth, or happiness. People seeking spiritual growth and enlightenment. For those facing challenges or difficulties in life, such as fear, stress, anxiety, or health issues, this bead gives them protection and courage. Those with a desire to fulfill their wishes and achieve their goals, as this bead grants them success and prosperity.",
      "wearingRules": "Rules for wearing and maintaining the Rudraksha Mala - Wash and oil the Rudraksha with almond oil once a month using a soft brush. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing it the next day. Remove it during sexual intercourse and funeral visits. You can remove it while eating non-vegetarian food or drinking alcohol and wear it again later. Women can wear it all the time, even during menstrual cycles, as per the scriptures. To energise it, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. Perform a Rudrabhishek of it when possible. Do not wear or use a Rudraksha Mala worn by others. Keep a separate Mala for Japa and for wearing."
