      "description": "Presiding Deity : Lord Ardhanareeshwar Ruling Planet : Moon Beej Mantra : Om Namah: Benefits : For unity, confidence, and peace of mind. Beneficial for ailments such as colds, coughs, headaches, depression, and neurological ailments as well as for good sleep. Origin : Nepal Description: What is the 2 Mukhi Rudraksha? The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha is a sacred bead with two natural lines or faces on its surface. It is also known as the Do Mukhi or Two-Faced Rudraksha. It symbolizes the unified companionship of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati, who are also known as Ardhanarishwara, the half-male and half-female form of the Supreme Lord. The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha represent the duality of creation and the balance of opposites. It is also the manifestation of the Moon, the ruling planet of this Rudraksha, and this planet influences the emotions, mind, and imagination. Wearing this bead helps diminish the negative effects of the moon, such as mood swings, depression, and lack of concentration. It also balances the material and spiritual aspects of human life, as well as the masculine and feminine energies within oneself. &nbsp;Our 2 Mukhi Rudraksha is available in collector, super collector, &amp; Haridwar sizes. About the ruling planet moon The ruling planet of 2 Mukhi Rudraksha is Chandra, considered the representation of the mind and emotions. The Moon is the source of light at night and influences the tides, seasons, and cycles of life. It is associated with intuition, imagination, creativity, and sensitivity. The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha helps balance and harmonize the effects of the moon in one’s horoscope. It can help overcome the challenges and obstacles that the Moon may bring, such as mood swings, depression, anxiety, and insecurity. It can also help enhance the positive qualities of the moon, such as love, compassion, empathy, and joy. Different ways to wear the 2 Mukhi Rudraksha The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha is a versatile piece of accessory. Some of the common ways to wear it are: The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand like a bracelet or around the neck. The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in popular combinations like the Siddha Mala, the Indra Mala, or the Maha Mrityunjay Mala. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report Checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer or our expert recommenders to choose a suitable one. Wearing them on a Monday morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity : As per ancient texts, there was a demon named Adi who could change his form at will. To entice Lord Shiva he approached him under the guise of Devi Parvati. Lord Shiva, the all-seeing God recognized this deceit and killed him. However, Goddess Parvati was furious to see another woman with Lord Shiva. She cursed Nandi, his gatekeeper to turn into a stone idol. Parvati’s fury knew no bounds. Lord Brahma decided to intervene and took away her dark, furious form (Kali). Parvati then took on a poised golden form called Gauri. Lord Brahma then blessed her and claimed her form would merge with her husband’s form so closely that nobody would ever separate both of her. This is how the Ardhanareeshwar form was first eulogized.",
      "benefits": "The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha has several benefits for the wearer, both spiritual and material. Some of the benefits are: Health Benefits: The bead is highly effective for sleep disorders, chronic cough and cold, and other problems related to the chest region. General Benefits: It enhances self-confidence and controls a wavering mindset, helping with decision-making and improving concentration. Spiritual Benefits: The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha is great for mental peace and fostering a calm demeanor. It helps channel the energy of the Svadhisthana Chakra, the second chakra located at the lower abdomen. It also helps attain devotion, detachment, and liberation from worldly attachments.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha bestows various benefits to the wearer. Some of the professions that can benefit from wearing this Rudraksha are: Teachers, counselors, therapists, healers, and mediators. Artists, writers, musicians, and actors. Businessmen, managers, and leaders. The 2 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn by people seeking harmony, creativity, communication, and cooperation in work and life.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
