      "wearingRules": "How to Care for Your Siddha Mala Clean the mala once a month with a soft brush and apply a little almond oil. Before wearing it again, chant “Om Namah Shivaya” 11 times. Remove it before attending a funeral or during intimate relations. If consuming alcohol or non-vegetarian food, you may remove it and wear it again afterwards. Women can wear the Siddha Mala during all phases of life, including menstruation. For regular energization, touch it to a Shivling and chant Om Namah Shivaya 11 times. A Rudrabhishek offers additional spiritual energization. Do not wear a Rudraksha that has already been worn by someone else. Keep separate malas for daily wear and mantra chanting (Japa). Avoid immersing the Mala in heavy liquids such as Ghee or Honey as they may enter the crevices of the bead and make it difficult to wear."
