      "description": "Presiding Deity: Lord Shiv Beej Mantra: Om Hreem Hreem Hum Hum Brahmaney Namah Benefits: Helps in harnessing both wealth and spiritual enhancement Origin: Nepal Description: What is the Sawar Rudraksha? The Sawar Rudraksha is a rare and auspicious bead with two beads naturally joined together, one with one face and the other with multiple faces. They symbolize the union of consciousness and matter, and the harmony of opposites. The Sawar Rudraksha bestows the wearer with the blessings of Lord Shiva and grants them success, wealth, happiness, and good health. It is worn by devotees of Lord Shiva, who worship him with the mantra “Om Namah Shivay”. It is one of the most revered and sought-after beads among the Rudraksha family, and it is a boon for those who wish to attain spiritual and material prosperity. What are the benefits of the Sawar Rudraksha? Different ways to wear the Sawar Rudraksha The Sawar Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The Sawar Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The Sawar Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combination like the Indra mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Lord Shiva was the supreme God of Hinduism, who was responsible for the creation, preservation, and destruction of the Universe. He was born from a cosmic fire that emerged from the eye of Lord Brahma, the creator God, who wanted to create a new being who could change and transform the world. He had three eyes, a crescent Moon, a trident, and a snake, and he married Sati, the goddess of fertility. He created many Gods and Goddesses, and many other beings and worlds. He was the Lord of the cosmic dance, the master of yoga and meditation, the patron of arts and sciences, and the protector of the downtrodden. He was worshipped by his devotees, who celebrated his festival of Mahashivaratri. He was one of the members of the Trimurti, along with Brahma and Vishnu. He was the God of mercy and kindness, who could grant any boon to his followers. He was the God of paradox and mystery, who contained both good and evil. He was the God of Shiva, the supreme being, who was beyond form and attributes.",
      "benefits": "The Sawar Rudraksha is a rare and powerful bead that consists of two Rudrakshas naturally fused, one of which has a single face or Mukhi. This Rudraksha bestows the wearer with the grace of Lord Shiva, the supreme destroyer and transformer. Here are some of the benefits of wearing the Sawar Rudraksha: General Benefits: &nbsp;Wearing it helps to gain property, wealth, and success in deals. It is also a good substitute for the elusive Nepal 1 Mukhi Rudraksha, which is considered the king of all Rudrakshas. Spiritual Benefits: The bead cleanses the sins of the wearer and purifies their soul. It also awakens the inner consciousness and induces spiritual evolution. It is ideal for those who seek the ultimate liberation and enlightenment.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The Sawar Rudraksha is suitable for anyone who wants to enjoy these benefits and live a prosperous life. However, it is especially beneficial for people who are in the following categories: One can wear it for success and harmony in your property or wealth. One can wear it for spiritual enlightenment and liberation by attaining the blessings of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati. One can also wear it for success and innovation by enhancing your intelligence, creativity, and leadership. One should wear it for protection and happiness by overcoming negative energies, evil forces, and diseases.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash and oil your Rudraksha with almond oil monthly using a soft brush and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing it the next day. Remove it during sexual intercourse and funeral visits. You can remove it while eating non-vegetarian food or drinking alcohol and wear it again later. Women can wear it all the time, even during their menstrual cycles. To energize it, touch it to a Shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. Perform a Rudrabhishek of it when possible. Do not wear or use a Rudraksha Mala worn by others. Keep a separate Mala for Japa and for wearing."
