      "description": "20 Mukhi Rudraksha Presiding Deity: Lord Brahma Ruling Planet: Moon Beej Mantra: Om Hreem Hreem Hum Hum Brahmaney Namah Benefits: Helps in harnessing both wealth and spiritual enhancement Origin: Nepal Description: What is the 20 Mukhi Rudraksha? The 20 Mukhi Rudraksha is a rare and sacred bead with 20 lines or facets on its surface. It represents the power of the Moon, the planet of emotions, mind, and creativity, and Lord Brahma, the creator of the universe. This Rudraksha is said to confer the blessings of the supreme creator, who is the source of all knowledge, wisdom, and art. The wearer of this Rudraksha is endowed with the ability to manifest their desires, achieve excellence in their chosen field, and enjoy a harmonious and prosperous life. The ruling planet of the 20 Mukhi Rudraksha, the Moon, influences the subconscious mind, intuition, and imagination, while its connection with Lord Brahma enhances intellect, memory, and learning capacity. Wearing this Rudraksha is believed to bring the grace of both the Moon and Lord Brahma, making it a highly auspicious choice for anyone seeking to explore their creative potential and realize their divine purpose. The 20 Mukhi Rudraksha is available in large and collector sizes.&nbsp; About the ruling planet Moon The ruling planet of the 20 Mukhi Rudraksha is the moon, which is also considered the representative of the mind and emotions. The moon is the source of light at night and influences the tides, seasons, and cycles of life. It is associated with intuition, imagination, creativity, and sensitivity. The 20 Mukhi Rudraksha helps balance and harmonize the effects of the moon in one’s horoscope. It can help overcome the challenges and obstacles that the moon may bring, such as mood swings, depression, anxiety, and insecurity. It can also help enhance the positive qualities of the moon, such as love, compassion, empathy, and joy. Different ways to wear a 20 Mukhi Rudraksha The 20 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The 20 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The 20 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combinations like the Indra mala, the Siddha mala, or the Maha Mrityunjay mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Lord Brahma, The Creator. These lines clearly state that Lord Brahma is Param Brahm, the Trimurti that performs the functions of creation, preservation, and dissolution. Here this energy is established as the supreme Purusha who is the embodiment of the supreme soul. As per the scriptures, the Trinity formed a very important aspect of worship. Lord Brahma known as Hiranyagarbha is the creator. Lord Vishnu is the preserver and Lord Shiva is considered to be the annihilator. This cycle continues in every Yuga. As per the Rig Veda, there is a supreme energy, which is the absolute source and is higher than each of the Trinity. This is what the Athar Veda addresses as Param Brahm.",
      "benefits": "This Rudraksha is said to confer the blessings of the supreme creator, who is the source of all knowledge, wisdom, and art. Here are some of the benefits of wearing the 20 Mukhi Rudraksha: General Benefits: Wearing it brings knowledge, visualization, and mental peace. It is a source of divine energy from various origins. Spiritual Benefits: The bead connects the wearer with the creator and expands the mind, intellect, and consciousness. It fulfills the desires of the wearer and helps in meditation and concentration. Health Benefits: It helps relieve stress, Alzheimer’s, bipolar disorders, and neurological ailments. It improves the brain function and health.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 20 Mukhi Rudraksha is suitable for anyone who wants to enjoy these benefits and live a prosperous life. However, it is especially beneficial for people who are in the following categories: People involved in land deals, property, real estate business, or any other business related to Earth. People who want to fulfill their desires and achieve their goals in life. People who want to overcome the obstacles and challenges in their lives and face them with courage and confidence. People who want to balance their Kapha dosha and improve their health and well-being. People who want to increase their connection with Mother Earth and nature and respect the environment.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
