      "benefits": "The Siddha Mala is designed to support every area of life. Invokes the blessings of all Gods and Goddesses. Helps strengthen the energies of the Navagrahas. Supports health, peace, prosperity and protection. Encourages success in career, business and personal growth. Helps balance all the Chakras of the body. Protects from negative energies and Nazar Dosh. Brings greater harmony to family life and relationships. Deepens meditation, mantra chanting and spiritual practice.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The Siddha Mala can be worn by anyone, regardless of age, gender, religion or background. It is especially suitable for: Those looking for one complete Rudraksha combination. Business owners, professionals and leaders seeking clarity and growth. People looking for protection and balance in daily life. Spiritual seekers wishing to deepen their practice. Those who already wear Rudraksha and want to experience a more complete combination.",
      "wearingRules": "How to Care for Your Siddha Mala Clean the mala once a month with a soft brush and apply a little almond oil. Before wearing it again, chant “Om Namah Shivaya” 11 times. Remove it before attending a funeral or during intimate relations. If consuming alcohol or non-vegetarian food, you may remove it and wear it again afterwards. Women can wear the Siddha Mala during all phases of life, including menstruation. For regular energization, touch it to a Shivling and chant Om Namah Shivaya 11 times. A Rudrabhishek offers additional spiritual energization. Do not wear a Rudraksha that has already been worn by someone else. Keep separate malas for daily wear and mantra chanting (Japa). Avoid immersing the Mala in heavy liquids such as Ghee or Honey as they may enter the crevices of the bead and make it difficult to wear."
