      "description": "1. Presiding Deity: Devi Durga 2. Ruling Planet:&nbsp; Ketu 3. Beej Mantra: Om Hreem Hum Namah: / ॐ ह्रीं हम नमः 4. Origin:&nbsp; Nepal About The Nine Mukhi Large Rudraksha reflects a stronger expression of Goddess Durga’s protective power. Blessed by the Nav Durga and Lord Bhairav, it supports people who handle pressure, leadership roles, or demanding responsibilities. This size helps maintain mental strength, fearlessness, and steady focus during challenging phases.",
      "benefits": "General: Strengthens confidence, resilience, and decision-making during demanding situations. Health: Helps maintain emotional balance, calmness, and consistent energy levels. Spiritual: Supports protection from negativity and strengthens inner awareness and discipline.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 9 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn by anyone who wants to overcome the challenges and hardships in life caused by their weaknesses or external factors. There is no restriction on who can wear this bead. However, some people who may benefit more from wearing the 9 Mukhi Rudraksha are: Great for women involved in professions that require them to harness the energy of Devi Durga. This Rudraksha helps them balance their personal and professional life, and achieve fame, prosperity, and artistic excellence. Those suffering from the negative effects of Ketu are the planet of detachment, spirituality, and enlightenment. This Rudraksha helps them reduce their fear, stress, and anxiety, and to gain clarity, wisdom, and satisfaction in life. Those who are seeking strength, courage, and confidence in their life. This Rudraksha helps them become powerful and self-confident and removes the fear of time and death. Those who are pursuing spiritual growth and enlightenment. This Rudraksha helps them connect with the divine power of Goddess Durga, and to surrender to her grace and guidance.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
