      "image": "images/cat-collector.png",
      "prices": {
        "INR": 1500000,
        "USD": 20000,
        "GBP": 1500000
      },
      "description": "Presiding Deity: Goddess Earth Ruling Planet: Mars Beej Mantra: Om Hreem Hoom Ekatvarupaye Hum Hreem Om Benefits: Expansion of existing business, launching of new venture, and good for land-related business. Origin: Nepal Description: What is the 18 Mukhi Rudraksha? The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha is a rare bead with 18 facets or lines. It is associated with the planet Mars and the goddess Earth. This Rudraksha represents the energy of the Earth element, which is the source of all life and abundance. The wearer of this Rudraksha is blessed with the qualities of stability, strength, courage, and perseverance. The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha also helps overcome obstacles and achieve success in all endeavors. It is beneficial for people involved in land, agriculture, mining, and construction. The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha is also known as the Bhumi Rudraksha, as it connects the wearer with the divine Mother Earth. The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha is available in large and collector sizes.&nbsp; About the ruling planet Mars The ruling planet of the 18 Mukhi Rudraksha is Jupiter, also known as Guru or Brihaspati in Vedic astrology. Jupiter is the planet of wisdom, expansion, generosity, and spirituality. It represents the fire element and the color yellow. Jupiter governs the signs of Sagittarius and Pisces and the ninth and twelfth houses in the horoscope. Jupiter can bring luck, fortune, optimism, and growth in one’s endeavors. However, it can also cause excessiveness, extravagance, arrogance, and dogmatism if it is afflicted or ill-placed. The 15 Mukhi Rudraksha helps balance and harmonize the effects of Jupiter in one’s horoscope. It can help overcome the challenges and obstacles that Jupiter may bring, such as lack of direction, confusion, overindulgence, and wastefulness. It can also help enhance the positive qualities of Jupiter, such as wisdom, creativity, communication, and spirituality. Different ways to wear the 18 Mukhi Rudraksha The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combinations like the Indra mala, the Siddha mala, or the Maha Mrityunjay mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Buying them from a trusted seller who can provide a certificate of authenticity and lab testing report checking their shape and origin Consulting an astrologer Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Bhumi Devi is depicted as the consort of Varaha (The boar form of Lord Vishnu). The Rakshasa Hiranyaksha torments Bhumi and her inhabitants. As a result, she sinks into the ocean. Lord Vishnu takes on the form of Varaha, dives into the ocean, kills Hiranyakashipu, and retrieves her on his Tusks. Thus Bhumi has the protection of Lord Vishnu at all times. Bhauma/ Mars / Mangal is the son of Bhumi Devi. He performed severe penance to Lord Shiva. Thus pleased Lord Shiva gifted Bhauma the Mangal Lok. Any Pradosh that falls on a Tuesday is also addressed as Bhauma Pradosh.",
      "benefits": "The 18 Mukhi Rudraksha is a bead that brings wealth, prosperity, and spiritual growth to the wearer. Here is a summary of the benefits of wearing the 18 Mukhi Rudraksha: General Benefits: It helps attain wealth and health. It is good for the land and real estate business. It is useful for business expansion. Spiritual Benefits: It activates and balances the Mooladhara and Manipura chakras. It improves digestion and metabolism. It enhances energy, willpower, and achievements. It can be worn with the Gayatri Mantra for spiritual growth. Health Benefits: It protects children and pregnant women from diseases and complications. It promotes a healthy and disease-free life.",
      "whoShouldWear": "&nbsp;Here are the types of people who can or should wear an 18 Mukhi rudraksha: People involved in land deals, property, real estate business, or any other business related to Earth. People who want to fulfill their desires and achieve their goals in life. People who want to overcome the obstacles and challenges in their lives and face them with courage and confidence. People who want to balance their Kalpa Dosha and improve their health and well-being. People who want to increase their connection with Mother Earth and nature and respect the environment.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
