      "description": "Presiding Deity: Lord Vishnu Ruling Planet: Sun Beej Mantra: Om Hreem Hum Namah Benefits: For good luck and fulfilling materialistic desires and for success and growth. Origin: Nepal Description: What is the 19 Mukhi Rudraksha? The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha is a highly revered bead with 19 lines on it, also known as Mukhis or Facets. It symbolizes the Sun, the source of all energy and light, and Lord Vishnu, the preserver and sustainer of the universe. This divine bead is known for its ability to bestow prosperity, courage, and success in all endeavors. It is particularly beneficial for those seeking to enhance their leadership qualities, confidence, and power. The ruling planet of the 19 Mukhi Rudraksha, the Sun, imparts vitality and radiance, while its association with Lord Vishnu promotes the maintenance of good health, wealth, and happiness. Wearing this Rudraksha is said to bring the blessings of both the Sun and Lord Vishnu, making it an auspicious choice for anyone seeking to illuminate their path with divine grace and wisdom. The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha is available in collector and super collector sizes.&nbsp; About the ruling planet Sun The ruling planet of the 19 Mukhi Rudraksha is the Sun, which is also representative of all planets. The Sun is the source of light, energy, and life. It is associated with vitality, courage, confidence, and authority. It also represents the self, the ego, and the soul. The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha helps to balance and harmonize the effects of the Sun in one’s horoscope. It can help to overcome the challenges and obstacles that the Sun may bring, such as arrogance, pride, anger, and jealousy. It can also help to enhance the positive qualities of the Sun, such as leadership, creativity, and enlightenment. Different ways to wear the 19 Mukhi Rudraksha The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in different ways depending on one’s preference and purpose. Some of the common ways are: The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn as a single bead or in combination with other Mukhi Rudraksha. It can be strung in a silk/wool thread or capped in silver or gold. It can be worn on either hand or around the neck. The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha can be worn in our popular combinations like the Indra mala, the Siddha Mala, or the Maha Mrityunjaya Mala.&nbsp; A personalized combination can be made by using the free recommendation of our experts to know which combination will provide you with the best outcomes. However, before wearing any of these ways, one should follow some guidelines and precautions, such as: Wearing them the next morning after taking a bath and wearing clean clothes Keeping them clean and dry Story about the presiding deity: Lord Vishnu is known to be the slayer of Daityas (evil entities). His favorite weapon for this is the Sudarshan Chakra wielded by him. In Mythology, this weapon of Vishnu is gifted to him by Lord Shiva himself. Once when Lord Vishnu found it difficult to defeat the Daityas, he meditated and prayed to Lord Shiva who is the ultimate destroyer of evil. Lord Shiva emerged and gifted him with the Sudarshan Chakra, a fabulous gold discus whose spokes emitted golden sun rays. Thus hundreds of Daityas were slayed every time Lord Vishnu unleashed this powerful weapon. Thus he vanquished negative forces to sustain life in the three worlds. Lord Vishnu is resplendent, silk-clad adorned with gold, and armed with weapons. Wherever he is present, evil is destroyed and Goddess Mahalaxmi bestows fortune. It is believed that those who follow the path illuminated by Sudarshan Chakra are directly led to Lord Vishnu.",
      "benefits": "The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha is a bead that brings wealth, prosperity, and spiritual growth to the wearer. It has the following benefits: General Benefits Balances all the chakras, creating harmony and positive energy flow. Promotes name, fame, and recognition in personal and professional life. Helps individuals excel in managing multiple businesses or income sources. Spiritual Benefits Anchors the wearer in the present moment, fostering mindfulness and awareness. Provides blessings from Lord Vishnu’s Dashavatar, enhancing wisdom, strength, and divine protection. Grants complete control over one’s thoughts and actions, leading to spiritual growth and clarity. Health Benefits Balances energies within the body, supporting overall well-being. Reduces stress and anxiety by harmonizing the mind and soul. Enhances focus, helping maintain mental clarity and calmness.",
      "whoShouldWear": "The 19 Mukhi Rudraksha is suitable for anyone who wants to enjoy these benefits and live a prosperous life. However, it is especially beneficial for people who are in the following categories: Lawyers and professionals in large law firms for success and recognition. Individuals seeking name, fame, and prosperity in their endeavors. Entrepreneurs managing multiple businesses or income streams. Spiritual seekers aiming for inner peace, self-control, and divine blessings.",
      "wearingRules": "Wash your Rudraksha with water and oil the Rudraksha using a soft brush preferably once a month using almond oil. Chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ before wearing the Mala the next day. Remove Rudraksha Mala while engaging in sexual intercourse and while visiting funeral grounds. We at Rudralife, suggest that one can remove Rudraksha Mala while consuming non vegetarian food and alcohol and wear it afterwards. Though our scriptures also highlight that they can be worn all the time without any restrictions. Women can wear Rudraksha and is their choice whether they wish to remove the Mala during menstrual cycles. As per our scriptures, there are no such restrictions and women can wear Rudraksha without any worries. To energise the Rudraksha Mala, touch it to a shivling and chant ‘Om Namah Shivaye’ 11 times. If possible, try to do a Rudrabhishek of the Rudraksha when possible. Do try to refrain from wearing a Rudraksha Mala worn by others and keep a Mala separate for Japa and for wearing."
